 ### CPU-based Shear-Warp
-A CPU-based implementation that uses RLE compression and Hounsfield scale classification to skip empty voxels. It compresses volume data using RLE for each coordinate axis and slice, classifies voxels using a linear transfer function with lower and upper bounds, and traverses data structures slice by slice, ignoring completely transparent runs. It does not use 3D data structures like octrees, unlike some original Shear-Warp paper variations [S5, unofficial].
+A CPU-based implementation that uses RLE compression and Hounsfield scale classification to skip empty voxels [S5, unofficial]. It compresses volume data using RLE for each coordinate axis and slice, classifies voxels using a linear transfer function with lower and upper bounds, and traverses data structures slice by slice, ignoring completely transparent runs [S5, unofficial]. It does not use 3D data structures like octrees, unlike some original Shear-Warp paper variations [S5, unofficial].
 
 ### Shear-Warp Factorization Rendered Examples Pipeline
-A hardware-accelerated pipeline implementation (SWF VRS) that includes a gradient processor, matrix multiplication processor, shader, and classifier. It applies a rotation transformation matrix, classification transfer functions (e.g., making soft tissues transparent to show bone), and a Phong fast lighting model. It supports perspective projections, front-to-back and back-to-front compositing, and front clipping for inside views, overcoming limitations of earlier hardware like VolumePro [S2, unofficial].
